    "dated": "2026-10-22",
    "about": "Austin Community College (ACC) and other Texas community colleges number courses with the Texas Common Course Numbering System (TCCN). This table is UT Austin's own list of the UT course each TCCN course transfers as. Credit is awarded only after UT evaluates an official transcript.",
    "notes": [
        "Lower-division biology credit may transfer as generic credit without a specific UT course number; applicability then needs department or dean approval.",
        "Some UT equivalents carry a different credit value than the UT course; substitution toward degree requirements can be at the academic dean's discretion.",
        "Texas community colleges have no direct equivalent of GOV 310L, 312L or 312P. GOVT 2305 + 2306 together fulfill core 070; either one combines with GOV 310L (but not with GOV 312L or 312P) to fulfill core 070."
